#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175806 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine"}] :question/id #uuid "8ffa8b1d-6651-594f-9c86-b4629d4cc2e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-759" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{(\\pi/3)^3}{3!} + \\dfrac{(\\pi/3)^5}{5!}-\\cdots + \\dfrac{(-1)^{n}(\\pi/3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+\\cdots\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x) = \\sin x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175807 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac85697c-557a-5b74-8046-79e9c345afc1" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Cosine"}] :question/id #uuid "8b102c11-e930-5b11-805a-1ff11cdb5995" :question/math-academy-id "e-760" :question/problem "Find the sum $1 - \\dfrac{9}{2!} + \\dfrac{81}{4!}-\\cdots + \\dfrac{(-1)^{n}3^{2n}}{(2n)!} \\,\\cdots \\,.$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x) = \\cos x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{1}{2!}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4!}{x}^{4}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3) & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{3}^{2n}}{(2n)!}\\,⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3) & =1-\\frac{9}{2!}+\\frac{81}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{3}^{2n}}{(2n)!}\\,⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\cos(3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058b950b-7211-5b63-a8ef-ca5da43d6e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538246} {:answer/id #uuid "3286958d-7c74-5b1d-87b0-93f4fb2b3417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538336} {:answer/id #uuid "8022af58-b7b6-5f7d-b6df-8a0168170bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538525} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c58dde-7497-55fd-9509-60437b98844f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538665} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ca12e2-aa98-5c4a-ba2d-ac826140d46c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8022af58-b7b6-5f7d-b6df-8a0168170bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538525} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccbfad55-03ca-511b-aff7-effb313d79ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b70f694-75c4-56a5-8060-3f93ae37aa40" :question/math-academy-id "q-103098" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac85697c-557a-5b74-8046-79e9c345afc1" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b6e35c-dea1-538c-98c8-0094d3f2c403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538338} {:answer/id #uuid "571409cc-60e9-5612-9926-6ed9afcda997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538417} {:answer/id #uuid "8d889743-ce2a-5980-a928-bf56bdaac70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538562} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0d5014-3b13-5aea-b08f-1fb39fc462a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538567} {:answer/id #uuid "ea987183-87c9-5540-a30a-3f341eb3b346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea987183-87c9-5540-a30a-3f341eb3b346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538768} :answer-field/id #uuid "2786ba38-c706-503a-8183-84ee0ea15a87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3922f3d0-9ec0-55ed-b2ff-7790813baa5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103114" :question/problem "$1-\\frac{25}{2!}+\\frac{625}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯=$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5 & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{5}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5 & =1-\\frac{25}{2!}+\\frac{625}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac85697c-557a-5b74-8046-79e9c345afc1" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277698a4-b642-5828-bd44-26f327d9872a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538311} {:answer/id #uuid "786f03b1-91d3-5f0b-98d1-31ea6b606b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538504} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8df014-f766-508e-ae02-8b1cf949fa8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538523} {:answer/id #uuid "a132b4e2-4cf1-5445-83d6-b3de269c66b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538616} {:answer/id #uuid "de32adf5-d49b-5e95-96c0-dc0ee2551230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "277698a4-b642-5828-bd44-26f327d9872a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538311} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf45e113-afc9-589f-ba9f-87e14316c2aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b2664ee6-8acb-52ad-889d-ed63a283e637" :question/math-academy-id "q-103117" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\,1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{64\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4\\,096\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯-\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{(\\pi /8)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(\\pi /8)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /8)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{{8}^{2}\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{{8}^{4}\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{64\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4\\,096\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac85697c-557a-5b74-8046-79e9c345afc1" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "725300ba-c2fd-5ef3-8e8b-23e9b44e688b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "725300ba-c2fd-5ef3-8e8b-23e9b44e688b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538489} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dea3e67-c006-5eec-a9a7-cb2408ce3d5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38c8627e-3005-599a-a37a-fb4e0aa52cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-350677" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac85697c-557a-5b74-8046-79e9c345afc1" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aacd782-dbd4-58d3-8bc5-764458467ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aacd782-dbd4-58d3-8bc5-764458467ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538513} :answer-field/id #uuid "e15e41c7-21f5-50db-bcda-4b29a0f68ef3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b7d68eb-3099-57db-9579-cc9c26274e37" :question/math-academy-id "q-350681" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\,1-\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{81\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{{(1/3)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(1/3)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(1/3)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{81\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9792a891-b2a8-5575-a93c-24bc7194cecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175187} {:answer/id #uuid "0bce1fbe-47f6-5c47-9ba0-df4ac06ddac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175191} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0c8ec8-308a-5fdc-8743-e14424b39b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538295} {:answer/id #uuid "5e61150a-84ad-5188-bc70-0933b2f92e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538438} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c1318f-c6a4-5e1b-8cbc-40f5c4a41b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e61150a-84ad-5188-bc70-0933b2f92e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538438} :answer-field/id #uuid "466627f8-aa23-5e1f-9d19-07970f3fffb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b610a1ae-13a4-52d6-8097-cd81c48ac52e" :question/math-academy-id "q-50897" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $-2+\\frac{8}{3!}-\\frac{32}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2) & =(-2)-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(-2)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 & =-2+\\frac{8}{3!}-\\frac{32}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c526c14-bb88-5ade-8041-886de05f49a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538472} {:answer/id #uuid "92108669-6093-5435-ba79-5169fa05995d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538575} {:answer/id #uuid "9a757735-7cc0-5dcf-90e7-545fc78fa434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538597} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4edf44-c7cf-53b5-b877-06a7a5da6527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538605} {:answer/id #uuid "d068f486-a976-58d2-8c3b-4190a273dbd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c526c14-bb88-5ade-8041-886de05f49a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538472} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa5b2ac-9ffb-5584-baa7-0c19b7707044" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f5058c8-bee4-550a-9863-d36cd2227082" :question/math-academy-id "q-50922" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\pi $ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "814f7c9d-5e49-5f4e-b1de-405ba981c35c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175199} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb8b45f-bf31-5954-9f4f-e885e74baf7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The series is divergent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175201} {:answer/id #uuid "5da6aadb-a542-5e5e-8757-2157556219f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175202} {:answer/id #uuid "50ea6359-ff35-5d40-ae48-09e30c47874b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{4+\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538407} {:answer/id #uuid "aba32c7c-b27a-52b9-8eda-752f04c9f073" :answer/type {:db/