ng $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{{(\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dce155a-cd12-5fa4-bab7-584e134737fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538395} {:answer/id #uuid "95d5509d-8326-5478-85bd-2640737f3409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538585} {:answer/id #uuid "998c4330-f85f-5d8e-8754-9eafbab12bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538594} {:answer/id #uuid "a53739e3-54c5-504e-b80e-c0b9e9d957ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538626} {:answer/id #uuid "a63e6faf-3df0-54ab-ad7d-d858e5ee7adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a53739e3-54c5-504e-b80e-c0b9e9d957ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538626} :answer-field/id #uuid "94017fed-3225-5f77-832c-3c6c4815c2e2"